mónica dr. Ajit Agarwal was an NHS  cardiologist for 40 years but he was  also a husband a dad and a granddad he  dedicated his life to medicine after  moving to the UK from India in his 20s  he died with kovat 19 aged 68 falling  ill just two days after retiring for his  daughters it was important he was  surrounded by his former colleagues this  is a handwritten note from the nurse who  took care of him he took the time to  write to us afterwards and she said I  wanted to let you know that he was not  on his own I held his hand that was  certainly no indication he was in any  pain  we used the patient profile to attempt  to him individually so I mean just the  just the fact that she must have an  incredibly busy job right now and took  the time to write that to us when we  couldn't be with him is really really  touching  the public admiration and respect felt  for health and care workers has been  clear to see and fear over the past ten  weeks but as the weekly applause starts  to fade and rainbows like these are  taken down some are asking whether we  need a lasting way to remember those  who've died that question has led to big  changes to a long-planned national  emergency services memorial renowned  sculptor Philip Jackson has  fundamentally changed his design to  incorporate the figure of a hospital  worker wearing full protective equipment  because of what has happened this  dreadful pandemic we decided that the  NHS side should be reinforced with the  secondary figure and so the ambulance  paramedic has now got a companion in the  nurse doctor figure the charity behind  the project is trying to raise three  million pounds to build it in central  London what we're seeing here is the  very best of our emergency services  brave men and women who are going out  putting their life on the line to save  you and me health unions have welcomed  plans  permanence recognition but warned the  priority now must be on protecting those  still risking their lives a sentiment  shared by Nikita and nimisha  I know what Dad would want and certainly  what I would like is to protect those  health care workers he was still on the  frontline that is the best way to honor  those who have died is to protect their  colleagues in their friends  KITT Bradshaw at Sky News in Suffolk
 

